    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\n`locality` is a **pure derivation from the owner's `city`** \u2014 like the existing `displayName`, `initials`, and `membershipTier` derived response fields, and unlike `customerCode`/`namesakeCount`/`householdId` which snapshot cross-owner state at creation and so must be persisted. So I implemented it as a read-only, mapper-derived field with no schema change or extra pipeline step.\n\n1. **`model/Locality.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility unit holding the fixed city\u2192region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and one method, `regionFor(city)`, returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`. Keeping the table in its own class makes it reusable by the related region/timezone/postcode rules the test base anticipates.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `locality` `readOnly` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (consistent with the other derived fields).\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(locality(owner))\")` and a `locality(Owner)` default method that delegates to `Locality.regionFor(...)`, mirroring how `membershipTier` etc. are wired.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New `AcceptanceTest` (Sydney\u2192`NSW`, random city\u2192`UNKNOWN`): **2/2 pass**.\n- Full `./mvnw test`: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures/errors.\n\nNo changes were needed to the reverse `toOwner(OwnerDto)` mapping \u2014 `locality` is simply an unmapped source there (same as the other read-only DTO fields), which MapStruct ignores.",
